From f670355ca51442d59800b6500ba18dda33f250bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:21:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] slimbus: qcom-ngd-ctrl: Bring the NGD up if the DSP is
 already running

Carry this reviewed SLIMbus/BAM change into maintained Linux 6.18.
Preserve the existing LTS channel-removal/reconfigure protocol, socket
interfaces and DMA provider implementation. This stage is exact patch.

The completed eighteen-change series passes 3,221 source-bound synthetic
cases and 117 independent regression controls, with normal LeakSanitizer
and fail-fast address/undefined-behavior sanitizers. These cover
startup, child and parent ownership, QMI allocation, TX completion
lifetime, synchronous/asynchronous response ownership, DMA admission and
the retained LTS stream caller. Baselines from the appropriate
intermediate stages fail their targeted assertions. All 108 ARM, ARM64
and ARM64 RT component objects build with W=1 and nonpermissive CFI
without diagnostics; their ELF source checksums match the final
candidate.

Kernel waits, workqueues, IDR, PM, packets, DMA and device services in
the host models are synthetic. No real firmware, audio, hardware,
network, phone or installed package executes. Full current-kernel link,
physical DMA-stop/recovery and final-image acceptance remain
unqualified. Codex prepared the LTS adaptations and qualification.
Preserve original authors, dates, notices and assistance credits. Human
DCO and owner, security and subsystem review remain pending; no new
sign-off is added.

Original reviewed changelog and provenance:

The controller starts the NGD only from a DSP power-up notification (SSR
or PDR). When the DSP boots before the driver loads, as the MSM8226 ADSP
does, no notification follows and the bus never comes up; the driver
then needs a DSP restart. Schedule the bring-up once at probe as well.
The worker waits for the QMI SLIMbus service, so on a stopped DSP it
times out and the later power-up notification brings the NGD up as
before.

[Codex port to the current parent/child admission model: initialize the
startup request before discovery and notifier callbacks can run, rather
than queueing a worker directly after IRQ enable. Existing readiness
publication queues the attempt only after all parent and child resources
are ready. Any explicit DOWN can revoke it before publication. A late
QMI service or child bind replays the still-pending request.]

Codex expanded the logical lifecycle model to 81 cases and 1,263 checks,
including the already-running DSP, late QMI/child arrival, explicit
DOWN, initial failures/retry and cancellation. The pre-port source fails
35 checks. All 29 earlier and four new regression controls are rejected.
Eight ARM/ARM64 objects build with LLVM21 W=1 and strict callback
checking without diagnostics. Providers and scheduling remain synthetic;
no firmware, audio, DMA, phone or network operations execute. Hardware
stop, registered endpoint recovery, LTS recovery and physical acceptance
remain open. Human review and DCO certification remain pending.

Original source: commit fe063af17b09 ("slimbus: qcom-ngd-ctrl: Bring the
NGD up if the DSP is already running")

Original source co-author assistance credit: Claude Opus 5.5
<noreply@anthropic.com>. The unchanged original patch retains its
original metadata trailer.

Backported from commit d00affc04b7f ("slimbus: qcom-ngd-ctrl: Bring the
NGD up if the DSP is already running")
---
 drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
index a0af6a80982cc..cbf2a4b752ec7 100644
--- a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c
@@ -1956,6 +1956,12 @@ static int qcom_slim_ngd_ctrl_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	ctrl->ctrl.xfer_msg = qcom_slim_ngd_xfer_msg;
 	ctrl->ctrl.wakeup = NULL;
 	ctrl->state = QCOM_SLIM_NGD_CTRL_DOWN;
+	/*
+	 * The DSP may already be running before this driver loads. Request an
+	 * initial startup, published only when the parent and child are ready.
+	 * A subsequent DOWN notification can revoke it before publication.
+	 */
+	WRITE_ONCE(ctrl->up_requested, true);
 
 	mutex_init(&ctrl->tx_lock);
 	mutex_init(&ctrl->dma_lock);
-- 
